                        "developer_response": "As we read your review now, we noticed, that you not really meant our Steam Accout, you just meant the way our company name has been written at different products. Yes, as a matter of fact, several publisher wrote our company name a bit different. Rondomedia wrote us as \"VIS - Visual Imagination Software\" (VIS means Visual Imagination Software, and one year after the founding of our company we only called us VIS-Games). On the the Steam shop page for Pineview Drive, UIG made a mistakte an wrote their own name as developer. We just adviced them to change this and now you can also read VIS-Games as developer for Pineview Drive on the shop page. For our latest productions you can always read \"VIS-Games\" and for our game Obscuritas the publisher simply the publisher wrote our name as \"VIS Games\" without the \"-\" in the name. This all happened as the publishers set up the Steam shop pages. All of our games are listed on our own webpage (http//www.vis-games.de) and we never changed our name to hide any of our older production! We are a serious game developer for more than 15 years now with more than 100 titles produced on several systems for several publishers! \nAnd at least, such speculations don´t belong into a Steam game review! If you have any questions, please simply contact us!\nWe never say anything against the personal opinion to our of our games, but please don´t start misleading speculations, if you just don´t understand simple facts.",
